1
00:00:00,126 --> 00:00:03,087
I didn't burn down the factory!

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:05,756
I knew they'd include you
in the investigation.

3
00:00:06,507 --> 00:00:10,428
And I couldn't risk them destroying you.

4
00:00:10,511 --> 00:00:12,847
None of this is your fault, dear.

5
00:00:13,389 --> 00:00:16,809
I know he's the vermin
that's infesting La Familia.

6
00:00:17,143 --> 00:00:18,644
Are you having someone tail me?

7
00:00:18,728 --> 00:00:20,229
I need to know the truth.

8
00:00:20,312 --> 00:00:22,022
Those are personal details.

9
00:00:22,106 --> 00:00:24,316
I can't help but be suspicious.

10
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:25,943
My resignation letter.

11
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:28,195
Diana, I can't stay in a place…

12
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:30,281
where no one trusts me.

13
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:32,241
Ricardo.

14
00:00:34,118 --> 00:00:35,119
Diana.

15
00:00:39,749 --> 00:00:40,833
Diana…

16
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:42,668
Hi.

17
00:00:46,422 --> 00:00:48,132
Diana, this is Sandra.

18
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:51,177
Ricardo's ex.

19
00:00:55,431 --> 00:00:57,349
I hope I'm not interrupting.

20
00:00:57,433 --> 00:00:58,893
I was just passing by.

21
00:01:00,352 --> 00:01:04,106
No, not at all.
Actually, we haven't even ordered yet, so…

22
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:05,649
Why don't you join us?

23
00:01:05,733 --> 00:01:06,901
I'll pass.

24
00:01:08,944 --> 00:01:10,863
Please join us.

25
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:14,074
I've heard so much about you.

26
00:01:14,909 --> 00:01:16,160
Really?

27
00:01:18,996 --> 00:01:21,415
Diana, Sandra's here
because she found out about…

28
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:24,210
my mother.

29
00:01:27,505 --> 00:01:29,882
And she heard that I'm selling my house.

30
00:01:30,508 --> 00:01:33,260
Yes, I heard.
I feel sorry for Ma'am Ester.

31
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:34,804
But, anyway, um…

32
00:01:35,596 --> 00:01:38,808
The property is under Ricardo's name, and…

33
00:01:39,475 --> 00:01:41,602
since we're both investors,

34
00:01:41,685 --> 00:01:43,938
we were just discussing
how we'd split the proceeds

35
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:45,606
once the property is sold.

36
00:01:48,067 --> 00:01:49,443
You're selling your house?

37
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:53,948
Yes. I guess because he's so affected
by his loss,

38
00:01:54,031 --> 00:01:55,908
he might want to go back to Indonesia.

39
00:01:59,703 --> 00:02:01,372
By the way, um…

40
00:02:01,580 --> 00:02:02,706
what are you doing here?

41
00:02:04,083 --> 00:02:05,334
I was really just passing by.

42
00:02:05,668 --> 00:02:07,795
There's something I need
to buy from this restaurant.

43
00:02:07,878 --> 00:02:08,963
I didn't know you'd be here.

44
00:02:09,046 --> 00:02:10,756
Please join us.

45
00:02:11,298 --> 00:02:12,383
Please.

46
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:14,468
I need to go to the restroom.

47
00:02:31,944 --> 00:02:33,237
I needed to go to the restroom, too.

48
00:02:47,543 --> 00:02:48,544
Why?

49
00:02:51,213 --> 00:02:52,214
Nothing.

50
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:55,593
I know what's going on
between you and Ricardo.

51
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:56,677
He told me.

52
00:02:57,219 --> 00:02:59,680
I also know you were surprised to see me.

53
00:02:59,889 --> 00:03:03,517
I'm sure Ricardo doesn't
talk about me much.

54
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:05,311
You're right.

55
00:03:07,563 --> 00:03:09,648
Well, that's how Ricardo is.

56
00:03:09,732 --> 00:03:12,151
He's very private about his personal life.

57
00:03:13,736 --> 00:03:17,823
All I know is that you two were
never really together.

58
00:03:18,699 --> 00:03:21,076
Except that you became
the mother of his child.

59
00:03:22,161 --> 00:03:25,289
I just didn't know you were still
seeing each other,

60
00:03:26,081 --> 00:03:28,876
that… you were still friends.

61
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:31,921
You've got it all wrong, okay?

62
00:03:33,047 --> 00:03:35,591
I won't be a problem for you, I promise.

63
00:03:35,674 --> 00:03:37,801
Ricardo's really just a good friend.

64
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:39,386
That's it. That's all there is to it.

65
00:03:40,721 --> 00:03:43,265
I don't think you need
to explain yourself to me.

66
00:03:44,391 --> 00:03:45,643
Besides…

67
00:03:46,644 --> 00:03:49,396
Ricardo's leaving. Right?

68
00:03:49,855 --> 00:03:51,482
You're not going to stop him?

69
00:03:58,948 --> 00:04:01,408
I understand how you feel, Diana,

70
00:04:01,492 --> 00:04:02,993
because I'm a woman, too.

71
00:04:03,994 --> 00:04:07,498
Whatever happened between
Ricardo and me back then,

72
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:08,958
that's all it was.

73
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:12,086
It didn't work out for us as a couple,

74
00:04:12,169 --> 00:04:15,756
but he's the best person I know.

75
00:04:17,591 --> 00:04:19,343
And I really do hope that someday,

76
00:04:19,426 --> 00:04:22,888
he finds someone who'll love him
the way he deserves.

77
00:04:23,347 --> 00:04:25,224
Because he's an amazing guy.

78
00:04:25,683 --> 00:04:28,477
And he deserves to be
with the best person.

79
00:04:37,736 --> 00:04:38,737
Diana!

80
00:04:40,072 --> 00:04:41,073
Diana.

81
00:04:46,495 --> 00:04:48,038
I thought you were joining us?

82
00:04:48,247 --> 00:04:50,207
Uh, no, I need to go.

83
00:04:51,417 --> 00:04:52,418
Diana, wait.

84
00:04:55,504 --> 00:04:57,131
Why are you following me?

85
00:04:59,133 --> 00:05:00,134
Didn't I tell you that

86
00:05:00,217 --> 00:05:03,053
if there's something
you want to know about me,

87
00:05:03,137 --> 00:05:05,139
you can ask me directly?

88
00:05:06,056 --> 00:05:07,725
I'll tell you the truth.

89
00:05:09,727 --> 00:05:12,896
I'm sorry. I don't…
I don't know what's gotten into me.

90
00:05:13,397 --> 00:05:15,774
I just want all of this to be over.

91
00:05:16,191 --> 00:05:17,443
Then let's end it.

92
00:05:19,361 --> 00:05:23,240
Whatever's been bothering me about you.

93
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:26,368
Diana, I've shown you everything

94
00:05:26,452 --> 00:05:27,619
you need to see.

95
00:05:29,747 --> 00:05:31,331
You're the only one
who refuses to believe me.

96
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:34,793
I'm not doing anything wrong to you.

97
00:05:35,836 --> 00:05:37,963
I really do love you. That's all.

98
00:05:39,298 --> 00:05:42,509
But you can't make me pay
for everyone who's ever hurt you.

99
00:05:44,219 --> 00:05:45,846
You know what hurts?

100
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:52,561
The part where you say you trust me,

101
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,273
but you're investigating me?

102
00:05:57,524 --> 00:05:58,692
I'm sorry.

103
00:05:58,776 --> 00:06:01,070
Instead of asking me for the truth.

104
00:06:02,571 --> 00:06:04,531
I thought what we had was real.

105
00:06:07,242 --> 00:06:09,495
Maybe it's time for me to distance myself,

106
00:06:10,496 --> 00:06:12,414
so you won't be confused anymore.

107
00:06:13,457 --> 00:06:16,960
I'll just use my remaining month
as vacation leave.

108
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:21,548
So you won't have to worry anymore.

109
00:06:25,302 --> 00:06:27,554
This is the last day you'll see me.

110
00:06:32,893 --> 00:06:34,478
Thank you for everything.

111
00:08:24,004 --> 00:08:25,589
Are you waiting for someone?

112
00:08:30,052 --> 00:08:34,139
Aww, Ricardo resigned.

113
00:08:36,725 --> 00:08:37,726
Hmm.

114
00:08:39,686 --> 00:08:42,689
Call Mr. Borja and the rest of the team.

115
00:08:44,274 --> 00:08:47,194
I already told them before I came in here.

116
00:08:49,488 --> 00:08:51,907
What about Ricardo?

117
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:54,368
Hmm, should I follow up with him?

118
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:57,913
Don't you have anything to do
in this meeting?

119
00:08:58,372 --> 00:09:00,666
Why don't you make yourself useful?

120
00:09:00,999 --> 00:09:03,293
I can't blame that guy.

121
00:09:03,585 --> 00:09:07,172
Because who could last in La Familia?

122
00:09:07,381 --> 00:09:08,548
Or with you?

123
00:09:12,511 --> 00:09:13,512
Hmm.

124
00:09:14,972 --> 00:09:16,598
Do you want some tea?

125
00:09:18,225 --> 00:09:19,309
Hm?

126
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:21,728
I'll get you some. Want some?

127
00:09:25,232 --> 00:09:26,608
Good afternoon.

128
00:09:28,527 --> 00:09:29,653
Did you call for me?

129
00:09:30,904 --> 00:09:31,905
You can go.

130
00:09:40,831 --> 00:09:45,294
Um… You're needed for the PR presentation
of Burger City later.

131
00:09:47,045 --> 00:09:50,048
I've already handed
everything over to the team.

132
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:58,307
Burger City requested
specifically for you.

133
00:09:58,390 --> 00:10:00,684
After all, you spearheaded the campaign.

134
00:10:01,268 --> 00:10:03,562
And when I spoke to your team earlier,

135
00:10:03,645 --> 00:10:06,481
I could tell they weren't ready.

136
00:10:06,565 --> 00:10:07,983
They weren't confident.

137
00:10:10,861 --> 00:10:12,612
Okay. I'll talk to my team now.

138
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:15,574
Ricardo, I need you.

139
00:10:16,742 --> 00:10:18,201
I mean to…

140
00:10:19,536 --> 00:10:22,831
be here in the meeting.

141
00:10:23,832 --> 00:10:26,710
After all, you're still serving
your 30-day notice.

142
00:10:27,127 --> 00:10:28,462
Just attend the meeting.

143
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:32,758
Okay.

144
00:10:59,951 --> 00:11:02,454
Under the law, an employee

145
00:11:02,788 --> 00:11:05,999
who engages in secret transactions

146
00:11:06,083 --> 00:11:08,835
against the company
can be terminated on those grounds.

147
00:11:09,586 --> 00:11:12,172
This should take effect immediately,
Sir Teddy.

148
00:11:14,383 --> 00:11:16,385
I have shares in this company.

149
00:11:16,468 --> 00:11:19,554
Being an employee and being a shareholder
are separate matters under the law.

150
00:11:19,930 --> 00:11:21,473
So you still retain your shares.

151
00:11:21,556 --> 00:11:23,225
It depends on what's stated

152
00:11:23,308 --> 00:11:25,769
in La Familia's buyback clause
in the bylaws.

153
00:11:29,356 --> 00:11:31,566
Thank you for attending the meeting.

154
00:11:32,859 --> 00:11:35,195
Actually, I wanted to talk to you, too.

155
00:11:35,278 --> 00:11:36,279
Diana!

156
00:11:37,322 --> 00:11:38,573
-Let's talk.
-Teddy?

157
00:11:38,657 --> 00:11:39,658
-Sir Teddy. Sir Teddy!
-No, no, no!

158
00:11:39,741 --> 00:11:41,034
-I need to talk to her!
-Teddy! Teddy.

159
00:11:41,368 --> 00:11:43,328
The investigation went through
the proper process.

160
00:11:43,412 --> 00:11:44,579
There was nothing I could do.

161
00:11:44,663 --> 00:11:46,790
If you want to appeal, get a lawyer.

162
00:11:46,873 --> 00:11:49,167
We'll go through the proper process.

163
00:11:49,251 --> 00:11:50,710
But for now, there's nothing I can do.

164
00:11:51,253 --> 00:11:53,213
Ricardo was the one behind all of it!

165
00:11:53,296 --> 00:11:54,756
Teddy, will you stop it?

166
00:11:54,965 --> 00:11:56,466
-Enough.
-Sis.

167
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,677
I'm trying to protect you
because you're my sister.

168
00:11:59,678 --> 00:12:00,762
But the truth will come out eventually.

169
00:12:00,846 --> 00:12:03,682
And when it does,
I hope you won't regret this.

170
00:12:03,765 --> 00:12:06,435
Everything you're doing,
I just hope it's not too late.

171
00:12:07,144 --> 00:12:09,855
-Teddy, just leave.
-Shut up.

172
00:12:09,938 --> 00:12:11,022
I'm not talking to you.

173
00:12:12,315 --> 00:12:14,192
I'll expose who you really are.

174
00:12:15,944 --> 00:12:16,945
Sir.

175
00:12:18,029 --> 00:12:19,322
-Just come with us, sir.
-Let me go!

176
00:12:19,406 --> 00:12:21,116
-I said let me go! Why are you--
-Don't worry.

177
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:22,409
-I'll handle this.
-Back off!

178
00:12:22,492 --> 00:12:23,743
Let me go!

179
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:32,252
Mom. Mom, are you okay?

180
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:38,550
Are you sure with your decision
about Uncle Teddy?

181
00:12:39,426 --> 00:12:42,596
His claims seem valid
and he can back them up.

182
00:12:45,307 --> 00:12:47,476
This isn't easy for me, too.

183
00:12:49,186 --> 00:12:50,520
But I think it's for the best

184
00:12:50,604 --> 00:12:53,106
that he isn't in La Familia for now.

185
00:12:54,232 --> 00:12:56,151
Maybe he needs to stand on his own.

186
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:58,195
Maybe this is what he needs.

187
00:13:04,159 --> 00:13:05,994
I'll check on Ms. D, okay?

188
00:13:15,337 --> 00:13:17,005
-Let me go! Back off!
-Calm down, sir.

189
00:13:17,088 --> 00:13:19,549
-Just come with us.
-Damn it! You're hurting me!

190
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:21,259
-Sir--
-What the--

191
00:13:21,343 --> 00:13:23,345
I'll make you pay for this!

192
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:25,055
-Especially you!
-Leave his things here.

193
00:13:33,146 --> 00:13:34,147
Put that down.

194
00:13:37,275 --> 00:13:38,276
You bastard.

195
00:13:39,152 --> 00:13:40,237
You're an animal. We're not done yet.

196
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,655
I will come for you

197
00:13:41,738 --> 00:13:44,115
and I will not stop!

198
00:13:46,618 --> 00:13:48,703
I'll expose all your dirt.

199
00:13:49,996 --> 00:13:51,248
I want to see you try.

200
00:13:52,958 --> 00:13:54,209
You'll surely regret it.

201
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:55,961
Get him out of here.

202
00:14:15,939 --> 00:14:16,940
Sorry.

203
00:14:17,732 --> 00:14:19,693
-Patricia.
-Enzo.

204
00:14:20,694 --> 00:14:21,945
How's Mom?

205
00:14:23,071 --> 00:14:25,115
She's fine. How about you?

206
00:14:25,615 --> 00:14:27,993
-How do you feel? Are you okay?
-I'm okay.

207
00:14:29,286 --> 00:14:30,287
But…

208
00:14:30,954 --> 00:14:32,038
But?

209
00:14:34,833 --> 00:14:39,087
I saw Sir Ricardo.
He escorted Uncle Teddy out.

210
00:14:40,338 --> 00:14:42,465
It's like he's having fun with it.

211
00:14:43,008 --> 00:14:47,429
The way he kicked Uncle Teddy out…
he was mean.

212
00:14:48,763 --> 00:14:50,515
I've never seen him like that before.

213
00:14:52,726 --> 00:14:54,352
It's concerning.

214
00:14:56,855 --> 00:14:58,940
You don't need to worry about it now.

215
00:14:59,316 --> 00:15:00,358
He resigned.

216
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:02,402
He won't be in La Familia for long.

217
00:15:03,111 --> 00:15:04,112
Okay?

218
00:15:08,116 --> 00:15:09,701
Teddy just left.

219
00:15:11,494 --> 00:15:13,246
Is there anything else you need from me?

220
00:15:15,665 --> 00:15:16,666
Let's go out.

221
00:15:17,417 --> 00:15:18,418
What?

222
00:15:18,793 --> 00:15:20,337
It's too chaotic in here.

223
00:15:21,046 --> 00:15:22,922
Besides, we have a lot to talk about.

224
00:15:23,673 --> 00:15:25,675
What happened earlier
was a lot to take in.

225
00:15:26,509 --> 00:15:28,386
I'm sure you need a break.

226
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:33,642
Diana, I don't have much time
left here in La Familia.

227
00:15:42,567 --> 00:15:43,568
Oh.

228
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:46,738
"Mother and child."

229
00:15:51,368 --> 00:15:52,369
Do you want it?

230
00:15:53,578 --> 00:15:55,205
It's beautiful.

231
00:15:58,500 --> 00:15:59,584
Excuse me.

232
00:16:01,753 --> 00:16:02,962
We'll get this.

233
00:16:04,172 --> 00:16:05,382
Ricardo.

234
00:16:05,465 --> 00:16:07,550
Ricardo, it's two million pesos.

235
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:08,968
It's okay.

236
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:10,428
It's my gift to you.

237
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,263
It's a good investment.

238
00:16:13,890 --> 00:16:16,017
I don't know. It's too much.

239
00:16:16,101 --> 00:16:17,185
Diana.

240
00:16:18,061 --> 00:16:20,146
You've been taking care of La Familia
your whole life.

241
00:16:20,438 --> 00:16:22,399
Maybe it's time to put yourself first.

242
00:16:23,483 --> 00:16:25,735
Take a load off your plate.

243
00:16:26,152 --> 00:16:29,489
Or maybe… it's time for you to step down.

244
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:35,036
I will stay with La Familia
as long as I'm needed.

245
00:16:35,578 --> 00:16:37,497
I made that promise to Dad.

246
00:16:38,164 --> 00:16:40,291
It's also for Patricia's future.

247
00:16:44,045 --> 00:16:46,464
You said we have something to talk about.

248
00:16:47,549 --> 00:16:48,591
Yes.

249
00:16:49,092 --> 00:16:50,802
Wait, let me go first.

250
00:16:51,386 --> 00:16:53,555
I need to say this and go first.

251
00:16:54,597 --> 00:16:55,932
Ricardo…

252
00:16:57,434 --> 00:17:01,855
I'm very, very sorry about
what happened at the restaurant.

253
00:17:01,938 --> 00:17:03,982
Forget it. It's fine. It's okay.

254
00:17:04,065 --> 00:17:05,442
-Are you sure?
-Yes.

255
00:17:06,234 --> 00:17:08,653
I invited you to go out because…

256
00:17:09,529 --> 00:17:12,782
because I want to be with you
in the little time we have left together.

257
00:17:14,659 --> 00:17:17,454
I want us to part
with just happy memories.

258
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:27,297
I'll miss you, Diana.

259
00:17:46,441 --> 00:17:48,735
It feels nice to see you smile.

260
00:17:50,987 --> 00:17:53,740
I can't even remember

261
00:17:53,823 --> 00:17:56,576
the last time I experienced this.

262
00:17:57,702 --> 00:17:59,454
And that song…

263
00:17:59,829 --> 00:18:03,082
Mom used to always play that on the piano.

264
00:18:08,588 --> 00:18:10,048
Ricardo, how have you been?

265
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:12,842
Oh, Rannie. Allan.

266
00:18:13,593 --> 00:18:16,805
Diana, these are
my ex-officemates in Indonesia.

267
00:18:16,888 --> 00:18:18,848
Rannie and Allan.
This is Ms. Diana Aragon.

268
00:18:19,349 --> 00:18:21,851
Diana Aragon of La Familia?

269
00:18:22,644 --> 00:18:23,728
Yes.

270
00:18:23,812 --> 00:18:25,605
What a surprise, Ricardo.

271
00:18:26,314 --> 00:18:28,399
We've never seen you go on a date.

272
00:18:28,483 --> 00:18:33,029
What a sight to see you
on a date with Diana Aragon.

273
00:18:33,404 --> 00:18:34,447
Am I right?

274
00:18:34,531 --> 00:18:35,573
The Chairmom.

275
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:37,951
I see your fetish is a dominant woman.

276
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:41,454
Must be pretty exciting,
isn't it, Ricardo?

277
00:18:41,538 --> 00:18:42,831
The Chairmom I'd like to--

278
00:18:42,914 --> 00:18:44,123
-Your face.
-What did you just say?

279
00:18:44,207 --> 00:18:46,209
-Easy, easy. Easy.
-Come on, say it again!

280
00:18:46,292 --> 00:18:48,545
-Ricardo.
-I'll beat the hell out of you!

281
00:18:48,837 --> 00:18:49,879
Easy, man.

282
00:18:49,963 --> 00:18:51,381
-What?
-Ricardo.

283
00:18:52,048 --> 00:18:53,383
Rannie, let's go. Let's go.

284
00:18:55,677 --> 00:18:57,011
My apologies.

285
00:18:58,179 --> 00:18:59,222
It's okay.

286
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:07,146
It's okay.

287
00:19:09,899 --> 00:19:10,984
I'm sorry.

288
00:19:11,276 --> 00:19:12,318
I'm sorry about that.

289
00:19:12,402 --> 00:19:14,612
I'm okay. It's okay. I'm okay.

290
00:19:16,406 --> 00:19:20,076
I won't let anyone
disrespect you like that.

291
00:19:21,286 --> 00:19:23,121
Diana I've never felt this way before.

292
00:19:24,038 --> 00:19:26,207
I know you're used
to protecting other people.

293
00:19:28,668 --> 00:19:30,545
But who will protect you?

294
00:19:31,629 --> 00:19:33,214
Who will protect you when I'm gone?

295
00:19:33,798 --> 00:19:36,843
Diana, if we don't feel the same way,

296
00:19:38,303 --> 00:19:39,804
then I won't force this.

297
00:19:41,014 --> 00:19:42,015
I'll just leave.

298
00:19:44,142 --> 00:19:45,727
I won't bother you anymore.

299
00:19:47,312 --> 00:19:48,897
Ricardo…

300
00:19:52,066 --> 00:19:54,277
I tried to stop it.

301
00:19:57,655 --> 00:19:59,198
But the truth is…

302
00:20:00,825 --> 00:20:02,994
I've never felt this way before.

303
00:20:19,385 --> 00:20:20,428
I'm sorry.

304
00:20:24,974 --> 00:20:27,310
-Carlota. Here you go.
-Oh!

305
00:20:28,019 --> 00:20:30,229
You brought the orders!

306
00:20:30,313 --> 00:20:33,858
Oh, my colleagues
have been waiting for this.

307
00:20:34,108 --> 00:20:35,610
There are new products in there.

308
00:20:35,693 --> 00:20:37,737
Tell them about it too.

309
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:39,697
There. Of course.

310
00:20:39,781 --> 00:20:43,660
Oh, after work,

311
00:20:43,743 --> 00:20:45,787
can we watch a movie?

312
00:20:46,037 --> 00:20:50,333
My favorite love team has a new film.

313
00:20:50,416 --> 00:20:53,419
And can we have dinner at a hotel?

314
00:20:53,836 --> 00:20:57,340
Oh! I think it'd be better
to spend the night there?

315
00:20:57,423 --> 00:20:58,424
Is that possible?

316
00:20:59,759 --> 00:21:02,553
-We can do that.
-Yay!

317
00:21:24,701 --> 00:21:26,160
I'm here.

318
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,834
It's from Ricardo.

319
00:21:44,804 --> 00:21:46,389
I know what you're thinking.

320
00:21:48,391 --> 00:21:50,059
It's Sir Ricardo.

321
00:21:50,476 --> 00:21:51,686
What about him?

322
00:21:55,189 --> 00:21:58,651
I just noticed that
he's like a different person.

323
00:21:59,193 --> 00:22:00,361
What do you mean?

324
00:22:01,821 --> 00:22:05,074
When you're with him, he's calm.

325
00:22:05,908 --> 00:22:07,368
He always finds a solution.

326
00:22:09,203 --> 00:22:12,457
But he acts differently
when you're not around.

327
00:22:13,499 --> 00:22:16,586
I understand if he's a private person

328
00:22:16,669 --> 00:22:19,172
and he has things
he wants to keep to himself.

329
00:22:20,423 --> 00:22:22,759
There are things we don't know about him.

330
00:22:23,176 --> 00:22:24,552
How can we prove

331
00:22:24,635 --> 00:22:27,597
that what he says is true?

332
00:22:29,390 --> 00:22:31,267
Well, what I would always say…

333
00:22:32,351 --> 00:22:34,771
be vigilant but fair.

334
00:22:34,854 --> 00:22:38,149
Even Uncle Teddy is suspicious of him.

335
00:22:38,941 --> 00:22:41,402
And Mom, I did my research too.

336
00:22:42,153 --> 00:22:47,408
I can't find anything about his family
or his personal life.

337
00:22:47,825 --> 00:22:49,118
Is that even possible?

338
00:22:50,119 --> 00:22:52,914
I already met the mother of his child.

339
00:22:53,122 --> 00:22:54,665
And his friends as well.

340
00:22:57,085 --> 00:22:59,128
I hear you.

341
00:23:00,254 --> 00:23:01,756
But let's be fair.

342
00:23:02,590 --> 00:23:05,051
If you guys are suspicious of Ricardo,

343
00:23:05,802 --> 00:23:07,970
then you have to have proof against him.

344
00:23:11,599 --> 00:23:13,142
-Huh?
-Oh?

345
00:23:13,559 --> 00:23:14,644
-What's that?
-What's happening?

346
00:23:14,727 --> 00:23:15,853
What's that?

347
00:23:16,395 --> 00:23:17,396
E…

348
00:23:18,147 --> 00:23:19,148
Enzo!

349
00:23:20,108 --> 00:23:23,444
Is there an earthquake or fire drill
scheduled today?

350
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:24,987
That's what I was wondering.
But there's none.

351
00:23:25,071 --> 00:23:26,239
I'm trying to call security now.

352
00:23:26,322 --> 00:23:27,490
What is that?

353
00:23:27,573 --> 00:23:29,325
Let's get out of the building.
It might be a real emergency.

354
00:23:29,408 --> 00:23:30,451
-Yes, yes.
-Let's go.

355
00:23:30,868 --> 00:23:31,869
Let's go.

356
00:23:37,792 --> 00:23:39,210
Maybe it's just a fire drill.

357
00:23:39,293 --> 00:23:41,838
No, we have to get out. It might be real.

358
00:23:46,092 --> 00:23:49,303
This is not right. Just hold on to me.

359
00:24:16,581 --> 00:24:18,082
Oh, Ricardo.

360
00:24:28,593 --> 00:24:29,594
Diana…

361
00:24:31,137 --> 00:24:32,889
I may be leaving La Familia…

362
00:24:34,140 --> 00:24:35,349
But I don't want to disappear
from your life.

363
00:24:41,230 --> 00:24:42,982
I want to prove my love for you.

364
00:24:44,650 --> 00:24:46,027
I love you so much.

365
00:24:48,529 --> 00:24:50,573
And I can prove that every day.

366
00:24:53,618 --> 00:24:54,702
Diana Aragon…

367
00:24:58,539 --> 00:24:59,874
Will you marry me?

368
00:25:26,651 --> 00:25:27,652
Diana.

369
00:25:28,778 --> 00:25:29,904
Will you marry me?

370
00:25:38,246 --> 00:25:39,372
Ricardo, get up.

371
00:25:46,712 --> 00:25:49,131
You know that I love you so much, right?

372
00:25:50,925 --> 00:25:53,302
Everything I've told you before is true.

373
00:25:53,803 --> 00:25:56,973
All of that. I love you.
I love you so much.

374
00:25:57,056 --> 00:25:58,057
But I'm…

375
00:25:59,892 --> 00:26:03,688
I'm not at the point of marriage yet.

376
00:26:06,065 --> 00:26:07,566
I can't.

377
00:26:08,150 --> 00:26:09,527
I can't.

378
00:26:10,444 --> 00:26:11,988
I'm so sorry.

379
00:26:50,026 --> 00:26:53,446
You seem relieved
that Ms. D rejected Sir Ricardo.

380
00:26:58,242 --> 00:27:02,371
A marriage… should be well-thought-out.

381
00:27:02,872 --> 00:27:03,914
It's not done carelessly.

382
00:27:05,750 --> 00:27:07,084
Yes. I know.

383
00:27:08,711 --> 00:27:09,879
But is that really the reason?

384
00:27:11,088 --> 00:27:12,715
Don't you want Ms. D to be happy?

385
00:27:14,925 --> 00:27:15,926
I do.

386
00:27:16,010 --> 00:27:18,346
What if it's Sir Ricardo
who could make her happy?

387
00:27:19,805 --> 00:27:21,223
No problem!

388
00:27:21,932 --> 00:27:28,314
As long as we're certain
that Sir Ricardo is a good man.

389
00:27:29,607 --> 00:27:30,649
You have a point.

390
00:27:31,942 --> 00:27:33,944
I also want Ms. D to be happy.

391
00:27:35,029 --> 00:27:38,866
And I do think it's too early
for her to say yes to Sir Ricardo.

392
00:27:39,492 --> 00:27:40,785
What I want is…

393
00:27:41,827 --> 00:27:44,872
if Mom will get another
partner in life again,

394
00:27:45,289 --> 00:27:48,000
it has to be someone
who will surely not deceive

395
00:27:48,542 --> 00:27:50,169
and hurt her.

396
00:28:01,138 --> 00:28:03,516
Oh, Dad! Is Mom not with you?

397
00:28:21,784 --> 00:28:23,285
Dad, is there a problem?

398
00:28:29,458 --> 00:28:31,210
Stop what you're doing for now.

399
00:28:31,836 --> 00:28:33,587
You have to help me do something.

400
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:43,139
Jena?

401
00:28:43,848 --> 00:28:45,266
April!

402
00:28:45,683 --> 00:28:47,101
Why is it so dark?

403
00:28:47,184 --> 00:28:49,979
Did they cut off our power?

404
00:28:50,479 --> 00:28:52,648
But the neighbors have lights.

405
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:54,984
Jena, April!

406
00:28:55,192 --> 00:28:56,569
Where are you?

407
00:29:06,871 --> 00:29:08,456
What is this?

408
00:29:17,715 --> 00:29:18,549
Martin?

409
00:29:35,483 --> 00:29:36,609
Carlota…

410
00:29:36,984 --> 00:29:38,277
let's get married.

411
00:29:42,323 --> 00:29:43,491
Why?

412
00:29:44,575 --> 00:29:46,577
Isn't this what you want?

413
00:29:46,869 --> 00:29:49,288
You've been waiting a long time
for us to get married.

414
00:29:50,706 --> 00:29:52,958
Is that your only reason?

415
00:29:54,126 --> 00:29:55,544
What other reason would I have?

416
00:29:56,378 --> 00:29:58,047
Mom, what's with you?

417
00:29:58,130 --> 00:29:59,757
Will you say no?

418
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:01,592
Mom, don't you want this?

419
00:30:04,637 --> 00:30:07,306
No, of course, I'm saying yes!

420
00:30:07,723 --> 00:30:09,225
Y-Yes.

421
00:30:09,517 --> 00:30:10,601
Yes.

422
00:30:18,943 --> 00:30:20,945
Yay!

423
00:30:21,028 --> 00:30:25,658
-Congrats, Mom!
-Congrats, Mom! Congrats, Dad!

424
00:30:26,867 --> 00:30:28,285
Patricia, Patricia!

425
00:30:28,369 --> 00:30:30,204
Your Dad and I are getting married!

426
00:30:39,421 --> 00:30:43,509
It seems like your marriage
with Diana won't push through.

427
00:30:44,176 --> 00:30:45,594
Patricia is against it.

428
00:30:46,303 --> 00:30:48,764
No one can stop my plan.

429
00:30:50,266 --> 00:30:51,350
Not even Patricia.

430
00:31:00,526 --> 00:31:01,777
Do you like it?

431
00:31:03,821 --> 00:31:05,531
Yes, but…

432
00:31:07,199 --> 00:31:08,993
It looks old, doesn't it?

433
00:31:09,076 --> 00:31:12,162
The color's kind of fading.

434
00:31:12,621 --> 00:31:15,583
Because it's secondhand.

435
00:31:15,666 --> 00:31:17,376
What matters is…

436
00:31:17,751 --> 00:31:19,545
I gave the ring to your mother.

437
00:31:20,713 --> 00:31:22,256
Besides, it's pretty, Mom.

438
00:31:22,339 --> 00:31:24,550
I'll start looking for a church.

439
00:31:25,426 --> 00:31:27,177
Sure. You can even start tomorrow.

440
00:31:27,553 --> 00:31:29,263
Wow! That's fast!

441
00:31:30,723 --> 00:31:33,225
Your father's just joking.

442
00:31:33,309 --> 00:31:35,728
We have to plan the wedding well

443
00:31:35,811 --> 00:31:40,441
because I want it to be
very extravagant. Right?

444
00:31:40,733 --> 00:31:44,278
I think it'd be better
if we have a civil wedding first.

445
00:31:44,528 --> 00:31:48,490
Then we can just do
the church wedding another time.

446
00:31:48,741 --> 00:31:52,995
It's like you're racing against someone.

447
00:31:56,749 --> 00:31:58,584
Well, would you look at it?

448
00:31:58,667 --> 00:32:00,628
I'm still the winner!

449
00:32:02,254 --> 00:32:03,464
What do you mean?

450
00:32:03,881 --> 00:32:07,259
Well, I'm getting married before Diana!

451
00:32:07,551 --> 00:32:10,512
Mom rejected Sir Ricardo's proposal.

452
00:32:19,063 --> 00:32:20,814
We're getting married!

453
00:32:40,501 --> 00:32:44,296
This! I want a ball gown.

454
00:32:44,380 --> 00:32:46,090
The train has to be long

455
00:32:46,173 --> 00:32:49,301
and has to be filled
with Swarovski crystals.

456
00:32:49,385 --> 00:32:53,180
Right? I want something that,

457
00:32:53,263 --> 00:32:55,891
when the people see me walking,
they'll go,

458
00:32:55,974 --> 00:32:59,269
"Oh, wow! Oh, wow, Carlota is beautiful."

459
00:32:59,353 --> 00:33:01,230
-Then they'll cry, right?
-Mom! Right!

460
00:33:01,313 --> 00:33:02,398
Right?

461
00:33:02,481 --> 00:33:03,565
-Correct!
-I want that. Yes.

462
00:33:03,649 --> 00:33:05,693
-We won't be outdone.
-Yes.

463
00:33:05,776 --> 00:33:08,737
But what if Ma'am Diana said yes?

464
00:33:08,821 --> 00:33:10,614
You would've gotten married
at the same time.

465
00:33:11,115 --> 00:33:12,991
I know, right!

466
00:33:13,075 --> 00:33:15,160
It's a good thing

467
00:33:15,244 --> 00:33:16,912
she rejected Ricardo

468
00:33:16,995 --> 00:33:19,498
because, if ever, my gosh!

469
00:33:19,581 --> 00:33:25,045
My gosh, your sister would've had
to share her inheritance with someone.

470
00:33:25,129 --> 00:33:29,883
What would happen
to the pain I endured for years

471
00:33:30,467 --> 00:33:33,429
if she wouldn't inherit everything?

472
00:33:33,887 --> 00:33:35,264
My gosh, Mom.

473
00:33:35,347 --> 00:33:37,558
Is that what you think of Patricia?

474
00:33:37,808 --> 00:33:40,728
Don't you treat her as your own child?

475
00:33:42,646 --> 00:33:44,898
But no matter what you say,

476
00:33:44,982 --> 00:33:48,110
I didn't give birth to her.

477
00:33:48,694 --> 00:33:50,154
Besides,

478
00:33:50,446 --> 00:33:54,199
if she weren't your father's daughter…

479
00:33:54,575 --> 00:33:58,328
If she weren't an heiress,
I wouldn't even glance at her.

480
00:33:58,495 --> 00:34:02,499
That's all she is to me.

481
00:34:03,792 --> 00:34:06,336
Come on, let's check out more gowns.

482
00:34:06,420 --> 00:34:07,713
-Here, Mom.
-I like that.

483
00:34:07,796 --> 00:34:10,090
-It's pretty.
-I think it suits you!

484
00:34:10,174 --> 00:34:11,675
I'll look slim!

485
00:34:13,010 --> 00:34:14,595
Oh, what's this?

486
00:34:15,053 --> 00:34:16,847
Wedding flower arrangements?

487
00:34:17,765 --> 00:34:19,641
Who's getting married?

488
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:21,810
Um, me, sir.

489
00:34:21,894 --> 00:34:24,480
I just got engaged, sir!

490
00:34:24,563 --> 00:34:27,608
Congratulations!

491
00:34:27,691 --> 00:34:28,734
Thank you.

492
00:34:28,817 --> 00:34:30,444
So, when is the big day?

493
00:34:30,527 --> 00:34:31,904
Very, very soon.

494
00:34:31,987 --> 00:34:34,782
And, of course,
you're going to be invited, sir!

495
00:34:34,865 --> 00:34:36,909
Oh, I'm sure you're very happy.

496
00:34:37,284 --> 00:34:38,911
Your husband's a lucky man.

497
00:34:39,369 --> 00:34:41,163
Very, very lucky, sir.

498
00:34:41,246 --> 00:34:47,211
Uh, do you have any advice
coming from a married man, sir?

499
00:34:47,795 --> 00:34:48,796
Well,

500
00:34:49,254 --> 00:34:52,508
I'm probably not the best person to ask.

501
00:34:52,591 --> 00:34:54,343
My marriage is, um…

502
00:34:54,676 --> 00:34:56,720
It has a lot of problems.

503
00:34:56,804 --> 00:34:58,597
I'm sure you can fix that, sir.

504
00:34:58,680 --> 00:34:59,973
I've tried, you know.

505
00:35:00,265 --> 00:35:03,018
But this one's not worth saving, so, um…

506
00:35:03,769 --> 00:35:05,437
I'm getting a divorce.

507
00:35:05,854 --> 00:35:07,439
Oh…

508
00:35:07,731 --> 00:35:08,899
Oh, no…

509
00:35:08,982 --> 00:35:12,611
I'm so sorry to hear that, sir.

510
00:35:12,945 --> 00:35:14,196
Oh…

511
00:35:15,155 --> 00:35:16,240
I'm okay.

512
00:35:17,741 --> 00:35:18,992
Patricia.

513
00:35:21,119 --> 00:35:23,455
Patricia! Hey. Hey.

514
00:35:27,876 --> 00:35:30,504
Could you get the invitations?

515
00:35:30,587 --> 00:35:35,717
The coordinator called to say
we should meet today, but…

516
00:35:36,093 --> 00:35:39,137
I have a lot of work to do.

517
00:35:39,930 --> 00:35:40,931
Okay?

518
00:35:42,140 --> 00:35:44,226
I'll do it when my shift's done.

519
00:35:44,518 --> 00:35:45,894
But, you know, it'll be quick.

520
00:35:45,978 --> 00:35:49,314
You can come back here
right away if you leave now.

521
00:35:49,731 --> 00:35:52,067
And pay for it too, will you?

522
00:35:52,150 --> 00:35:56,488
You haven't contributed anything
to our wedding, after all.

523
00:35:56,572 --> 00:35:57,573
Hm?

524
00:35:58,073 --> 00:36:00,492
Mom, Mom asked me to do something.

525
00:36:00,742 --> 00:36:01,952
So what?

526
00:36:02,369 --> 00:36:06,748
My marriage to your father
is not important to you?

527
00:36:06,832 --> 00:36:08,083
Is that it?

528
00:36:08,292 --> 00:36:09,751
Patricia.

529
00:36:10,961 --> 00:36:12,087
Is everything all right?

530
00:36:12,588 --> 00:36:13,672
I'm fine, Enzo.

531
00:36:16,633 --> 00:36:19,094
Mom, I really can't handle that today.

532
00:36:20,387 --> 00:36:22,472
We're working,
and that's a personal matter.

533
00:36:22,764 --> 00:36:26,727
I am asking you for such a small favor.

534
00:36:26,810 --> 00:36:29,021
And yet you can't do it.

535
00:36:31,064 --> 00:36:32,941
It's like we're not family.

536
00:36:33,275 --> 00:36:34,776
Sorry, with all due respect…

537
00:36:36,320 --> 00:36:39,072
Patricia does everything for you.

538
00:36:39,656 --> 00:36:44,578
Please don't say hurtful things to her
when she does something for herself.

539
00:36:44,912 --> 00:36:46,371
What did you say?

540
00:36:47,247 --> 00:36:48,498
Enzo…

541
00:36:49,124 --> 00:36:50,459
What is he talking--

542
00:36:51,460 --> 00:36:54,087
What have you been telling
this arrogant guy?

543
00:36:54,421 --> 00:36:55,714
Why is he talking to me like that?

544
00:36:55,797 --> 00:36:58,467
Have you been badmouthing me?

545
00:36:58,800 --> 00:36:59,927
Mom, people can hear you.

546
00:37:00,010 --> 00:37:04,264
And what right do you have
to talk to my daughter like that?

547
00:37:04,890 --> 00:37:05,891
Here?

548
00:37:09,645 --> 00:37:12,230
Wow! Wow!

549
00:37:13,106 --> 00:37:15,734
What a perfect mother!

550
00:37:16,401 --> 00:37:18,362
-Mom… that's enough.
-Go on.

551
00:37:18,946 --> 00:37:21,657
Do it. Make a scene.

552
00:37:22,074 --> 00:37:23,659
Show everyone your true colors.

553
00:37:23,742 --> 00:37:26,870
I'm not the one making a scene.

554
00:37:26,954 --> 00:37:28,080
You are!

555
00:37:28,372 --> 00:37:33,251
You're the one who humiliated a man
in front of so many people.

556
00:37:33,335 --> 00:37:34,544
Mom…

557
00:37:34,628 --> 00:37:35,796
Me?

558
00:37:38,298 --> 00:37:41,009
Martin and I are engaged!

559
00:37:42,260 --> 00:37:44,054
And you will die of envy!

560
00:37:44,554 --> 00:37:45,389
Mom…

561
00:37:45,764 --> 00:37:48,767
You're so shameless.

562
00:37:49,393 --> 00:37:51,979
Let go of me!

563
00:37:52,062 --> 00:37:55,691
Don't you dare lay a finger
on my daughter!

564
00:37:55,774 --> 00:37:58,568
I may have put up with everything,
but not that!

565
00:38:01,029 --> 00:38:03,323
You think you've taken
everything from me, Carlota?

566
00:38:03,740 --> 00:38:05,200
No matter what you do,

567
00:38:05,283 --> 00:38:08,286
you can't hide the truth.

568
00:38:08,745 --> 00:38:11,081
That you ruined my family

569
00:38:11,164 --> 00:38:15,002
when you chose to become
Martin's mistress.

570
00:38:25,387 --> 00:38:26,430
Mom…

571
00:38:27,973 --> 00:38:31,768
I thought you and Dad got together
after he and Mom broke up?

572
00:38:36,606 --> 00:38:37,607
Mom.

573
00:38:38,817 --> 00:38:39,985
Patricia…

574
00:38:40,944 --> 00:38:42,946
I raised you, didn't I?

575
00:38:43,030 --> 00:38:45,240
You should believe me.

576
00:38:46,241 --> 00:38:47,534
But what's the truth?

577
00:38:55,917 --> 00:38:58,420
You're shameless.

578
00:38:59,379 --> 00:39:01,715
Who's more shameless?

579
00:39:03,050 --> 00:39:06,178
I caught you and Martin
together back then.

580
00:39:07,304 --> 00:39:12,601
My husband and I split up
because of you, remember?

581
00:39:16,521 --> 00:39:20,025
You destroyed our family!

582
00:39:53,642 --> 00:39:54,893
I'm so sorry.

583
00:39:57,187 --> 00:39:58,355
I'm sorry, dear.

584
00:40:03,944 --> 00:40:05,737
Why aren't you all answering?

585
00:40:17,207 --> 00:40:18,750
Sweetie, what's wrong?

586
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:22,087
I thought you and Mom Carlota
only got together

587
00:40:22,170 --> 00:40:24,005
after you and Mom separated?

588
00:40:24,464 --> 00:40:26,091
Did you cheat on Mom?

589
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:29,010
It wasn't that simple, Patricia.

590
00:40:29,094 --> 00:40:33,348
I asked you a yes-or-no question, Dad.

591
00:40:34,307 --> 00:40:36,101
Your mother and I had been
having problems for a long time.

592
00:40:36,351 --> 00:40:37,769
She was always focused on the company.

593
00:40:37,853 --> 00:40:40,147
She stopped being a wife and a mother.

594
00:40:40,522 --> 00:40:41,565
You know that, don't you?

595
00:40:43,233 --> 00:40:46,653
Why didn't you just leave her
if you weren't happy anymore?

596
00:40:48,196 --> 00:40:50,323
Why did you have to cheat on her?

597
00:40:53,535 --> 00:40:56,872
I had to choose between the two of you.

598
00:40:58,373 --> 00:41:02,043
Do you know how hard it was for me?

599
00:41:02,919 --> 00:41:06,089
I chose you because I thought…

600
00:41:06,506 --> 00:41:09,092
Mom was the only one at fault.

601
00:41:09,926 --> 00:41:12,596
Why did you destroy our family?

602
00:41:13,680 --> 00:41:15,432
I thought you understood!

603
00:41:15,932 --> 00:41:18,602
You let me grow up without her.

604
00:41:19,019 --> 00:41:21,313
I've had to squeeze myself

605
00:41:21,396 --> 00:41:23,899
into the family you and Mom Carlota built!

606
00:41:24,274 --> 00:41:26,693
Patricia, you know that's not true.

607
00:41:26,776 --> 00:41:28,570
Carlota treats you like her own daughter!

608
00:41:29,529 --> 00:41:30,739
Come on, Pa…

609
00:41:32,365 --> 00:41:34,576
You know that's not true.

610
00:41:34,743 --> 00:41:37,996
She treats me differently
from her own children.

611
00:41:38,371 --> 00:41:40,665
But I understood that.

612
00:41:41,583 --> 00:41:43,585
I understood your situation.

613
00:41:43,668 --> 00:41:46,213
Because I didn't want
to make things harder for you.

614
00:41:46,296 --> 00:41:49,424
Because I wanted you to be happy.

615
00:41:49,674 --> 00:41:51,176
What's this, Patricia?

616
00:41:52,177 --> 00:41:56,056
Are you throwing a fit
because of what you found out?

617
00:42:03,772 --> 00:42:06,066
One word from your mother,

618
00:42:06,149 --> 00:42:07,943
and you've forgotten everything

619
00:42:08,276 --> 00:42:10,528
your Dad and I did for you?

620
00:42:10,612 --> 00:42:12,864
Why did you destroy our family?

621
00:42:13,365 --> 00:42:14,991
Why did you choose to be a mistress?

622
00:42:17,035 --> 00:42:18,119
Carlota!

623
00:42:18,203 --> 00:42:19,704
You ingrate!

624
00:42:20,288 --> 00:42:22,374
So what if I was a mistress?

625
00:42:23,625 --> 00:42:26,795
This mistress is the one who raised you!

626
00:42:26,878 --> 00:42:29,214
Are you going to forget all the sacrifices

627
00:42:29,297 --> 00:42:31,883
your Dad and I made for you?

628
00:42:31,967 --> 00:42:35,262
Who raised you from the time
you were a child?

629
00:42:36,471 --> 00:42:38,181
Well, I'm sorry.

630
00:42:40,225 --> 00:42:43,979
I convinced myself
that you saw me as your daughter.

631
00:42:44,062 --> 00:42:45,772
If you really saw me as your daughter,

632
00:42:45,855 --> 00:42:48,191
you wouldn't hold those things
over my head.

633
00:42:50,277 --> 00:42:52,779
How dare you talk back? Patricia!

634
00:42:52,946 --> 00:42:55,615
Why'd you have to hit Patricia?

635
00:42:56,658 --> 00:42:58,201
This is your fault.

636
00:42:58,285 --> 00:42:59,452
What are you saying?

637
00:42:59,869 --> 00:43:04,874
If you'd married me back then,
she wouldn't call me a mistress!

638
00:43:05,458 --> 00:43:08,044
You let me become the other woman!

639
00:43:55,842 --> 00:43:56,843
Patricia…

640
00:43:59,054 --> 00:44:00,472
Let me explain.

641
00:44:01,056 --> 00:44:03,141
I know you don't understand.

642
00:44:04,809 --> 00:44:05,894
I was scared.

643
00:44:07,395 --> 00:44:09,189
I didn't want you to hate me.

644
00:44:09,731 --> 00:44:11,316
I couldn't bear losing you.

645
00:44:18,990 --> 00:44:20,825
All my life, Dad…

646
00:44:21,326 --> 00:44:23,536
I did everything your family wanted.

647
00:44:26,539 --> 00:44:28,416
I gave everything I had…

648
00:44:32,128 --> 00:44:35,507
I gave everything I had,
even when I had nothing left.

649
00:44:37,175 --> 00:44:39,886
Because I thought…

650
00:44:40,970 --> 00:44:44,224
I'd be a part of your family
as long as I was useful to you.

651
00:44:44,766 --> 00:44:47,102
Patricia, that's not true.

652
00:44:47,394 --> 00:44:49,104
I love all of you…

653
00:44:52,232 --> 00:44:53,900
I love you so much, Dad.

654
00:44:56,903 --> 00:44:59,697
I want to believe
I made the right decision back then…

655
00:45:00,573 --> 00:45:02,617
when I chose to go with you.

656
00:45:03,576 --> 00:45:05,453
But did I make a mistake…

657
00:45:06,204 --> 00:45:09,124
in choosing you, Dad?

658
00:45:11,876 --> 00:45:14,879
I was angry at Mom for so long.

659
00:45:18,341 --> 00:45:20,635
I hated her for so long…

660
00:45:22,637 --> 00:45:23,721
Patricia, that's not true…

661
00:45:24,180 --> 00:45:26,182
Because I truly believed she was the one

662
00:45:26,266 --> 00:45:29,519
who destroyed our family.

663
00:45:30,103 --> 00:45:31,312
Why did you do that, Pa?

664
00:45:31,396 --> 00:45:33,982
Why did you lie to me?

665
00:45:35,942 --> 00:45:37,902
I only did that because…

666
00:45:38,653 --> 00:45:41,990
I was afraid of losing you.

667
00:45:42,282 --> 00:45:43,992
Your mother had everything.

668
00:45:46,369 --> 00:45:49,122
She could've easily taken you
away from me back then.

669
00:45:49,205 --> 00:45:50,373
I'm powerless.

670
00:45:51,124 --> 00:45:53,418
I had no chance against her.

671
00:45:54,294 --> 00:45:56,171
I had no chance.

672
00:45:56,921 --> 00:45:58,631
I'm sorry.

673
00:46:01,342 --> 00:46:02,302
Patricia…

674
00:46:05,805 --> 00:46:08,433
Is that really the reason, Dad?

675
00:46:10,643 --> 00:46:12,353
Or did you use me as a prize

676
00:46:12,437 --> 00:46:15,064
just so you could feel like
you'd won against Mom?

677
00:46:15,982 --> 00:46:17,775
No, dear. It's not like that.

678
00:46:31,706 --> 00:46:33,124
The initial terms look promising.

679
00:46:33,208 --> 00:46:34,209
Right, Ms. Aragon?

680
00:46:34,667 --> 00:46:37,003
So, I guess that's it for this meeting.

681
00:46:37,086 --> 00:46:38,171
-Okay.
-Thank you.

682
00:46:38,254 --> 00:46:39,255
Sure.

683
00:46:39,339 --> 00:46:40,507
-Let's go?
-Let's go.

684
00:46:46,387 --> 00:46:47,805
Benjie, I'm heading out now.

685
00:46:56,773 --> 00:46:57,815
Hi.

686
00:46:59,067 --> 00:47:00,109
Sandra.

687
00:47:00,401 --> 00:47:01,819
What are you doing here?

688
00:47:01,903 --> 00:47:05,740
Oh, I'm meeting a friend who's interested
in buying Ricardo's place.

689
00:47:05,823 --> 00:47:09,786
Ricardo had to leave earlier
than expected, so I'm handling the sale.

690
00:47:10,370 --> 00:47:11,788
Ricardo is leaving?

691
00:47:12,163 --> 00:47:15,667
Um, I actually called him,
and he is on his way to the airport.

692
00:47:20,255 --> 00:47:21,756
Didn't he tell you?

693
00:47:26,553 --> 00:47:28,179
ISABELLE CHAVEZ
BORN: AUG. 16 2007 DIED: OCT. 23 2022

694
00:47:31,307 --> 00:47:33,476
Uh… Excuse me.

695
00:47:38,523 --> 00:47:40,733
How are you related to the deceased?

696
00:47:41,401 --> 00:47:42,443
Who are you?

697
00:47:42,527 --> 00:47:44,487
I have a friend in the US.

698
00:47:45,029 --> 00:47:46,906
He said that his daughter is buried here.

699
00:47:47,198 --> 00:47:48,700
He wanted me to check.

700
00:47:49,075 --> 00:47:51,160
This one. Isabelle Chavez.

701
00:47:51,411 --> 00:47:54,205
We have no relatives in America.
You must have gotten it wrong.

702
00:47:58,418 --> 00:48:01,629
Ms. D, it looks like we won't be able
to get to the airport.

703
00:48:01,921 --> 00:48:03,298
The traffic is very heavy.

704
00:48:07,051 --> 00:48:08,761
Ma'am, I'm sorry.

705
00:48:08,845 --> 00:48:09,846
But are you sure?

706
00:48:09,929 --> 00:48:12,724
My friend told me
that his daughter died of cancer.

707
00:48:12,974 --> 00:48:14,684
My daughter died because of an accident.

708
00:48:14,767 --> 00:48:16,185
Who's the friend you're talking about?

709
00:48:16,769 --> 00:48:18,730
Ricardo Salvador? Do you know him?

710
00:48:19,230 --> 00:48:20,773
I don't know him.

711
00:48:20,857 --> 00:48:21,858
This guy.

712
00:48:26,321 --> 00:48:28,698
I'm sorry, but I really don't know him.

713
00:48:29,365 --> 00:48:30,366
What about you, sir?

714
00:48:30,783 --> 00:48:32,493
I've seen him before.

715
00:48:32,869 --> 00:48:35,872
I've seen him a few times
when I'd bring flowers

716
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:37,165
for your daughter, ma'am.

717
00:48:37,957 --> 00:48:39,834
There's a grave he visits.

718
00:48:40,251 --> 00:48:41,461
Then tell him.

719
00:48:41,544 --> 00:48:43,004
Sir, follow me.

720
00:48:45,131 --> 00:48:46,132
This one, sir.

721
00:48:47,258 --> 00:48:48,885
-Okay. Thank you.
-Okay.

722
00:49:02,565 --> 00:49:05,443
I made the recipe! It came from me!

723
00:49:05,526 --> 00:49:07,195
I'm telling the truth!

724
00:49:07,278 --> 00:49:08,279
You are thieves!

725
00:49:28,091 --> 00:49:29,133
Ricardo?

726
00:49:33,012 --> 00:49:34,013
Diana.

727
00:49:34,889 --> 00:49:36,683
I thought you already left.

728
00:49:37,725 --> 00:49:38,726
Why are you here?

729
00:49:40,311 --> 00:49:41,896
I-I don't know either.

730
00:49:44,816 --> 00:49:47,402
Diana, I don't know what you did to me.

731
00:49:47,694 --> 00:49:49,320
With everything that has happened to me,

732
00:49:49,612 --> 00:49:51,698
I have long accepted
that I will be alone in life.

733
00:49:53,116 --> 00:49:54,492
But because of you,

734
00:49:55,743 --> 00:49:57,995
I had the hope of being happy again.

735
00:49:58,871 --> 00:50:00,707
But now I feel…

736
00:50:03,418 --> 00:50:04,836
devastated.

737
00:50:08,131 --> 00:50:10,174
Because I'm not good enough
to be loved by you.

738
00:50:12,218 --> 00:50:15,471
I don't want you to feel that way.
I didn't mean to.

739
00:50:15,888 --> 00:50:17,473
I'm so sorry.

740
00:50:18,474 --> 00:50:21,352
You know, I don't want to go. But if…

741
00:50:22,311 --> 00:50:24,105
if I'm not worth anything to you anymore…

742
00:50:25,940 --> 00:50:28,651
there is no reason for me to stay here.

743
00:50:29,736 --> 00:50:30,778
I understand.

744
00:50:37,660 --> 00:50:38,953
Ricardo.

745
00:50:55,136 --> 00:50:56,137
Patricia.

746
00:50:56,637 --> 00:50:57,638
April.

747
00:51:00,975 --> 00:51:03,352
What's happening between you
and Mom and Dad?

748
00:51:03,561 --> 00:51:05,563
Mom said you had an argument.

749
00:51:07,023 --> 00:51:08,649
Don't worry about it.

750
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:10,401
It will pass.

751
00:51:10,485 --> 00:51:12,153
Patricia, are you mad at us?

752
00:51:13,029 --> 00:51:14,572
N-No.

753
00:51:14,655 --> 00:51:16,949
I know that you were hurt.

754
00:51:18,785 --> 00:51:22,371
But, Patricia, I want you to know that I…

755
00:51:24,582 --> 00:51:26,501
have never thought of you differently.

756
00:51:26,959 --> 00:51:28,544
You're my family.

757
00:51:32,548 --> 00:51:36,469
I know it's hard that you
have to be responsible for me and Jena.

758
00:51:37,887 --> 00:51:39,514
That's why I'm studying hard…

759
00:51:39,597 --> 00:51:42,183
so that when I graduate,

760
00:51:42,475 --> 00:51:43,935
I'll help you.

761
00:51:45,144 --> 00:51:49,941
So you can achieve your dreams
that you have set aside for our sake.

762
00:51:51,317 --> 00:51:56,572
I am so thankful
for all the sacrifices you made for us.

763
00:52:03,412 --> 00:52:06,415
That's so nice to hear.

764
00:52:08,000 --> 00:52:09,252
Hey.

765
00:52:11,838 --> 00:52:13,756
I did that…

766
00:52:14,674 --> 00:52:16,509
because I love you.

767
00:52:18,803 --> 00:52:20,555
You two are my sisters.

768
00:52:21,222 --> 00:52:25,101
And that will never change.

769
00:52:26,018 --> 00:52:27,395
Thank you, sis.

770
00:52:38,906 --> 00:52:39,907
Clara.

771
00:52:39,991 --> 00:52:41,117
-Yes?
-Has Mom arrived?

772
00:52:41,492 --> 00:52:43,160
She's not here yet.

773
00:52:43,578 --> 00:52:45,413
-Huh?
-What? Why isn't she here yet?

774
00:52:46,122 --> 00:52:49,417
I called and texted her,
but she wasn't answering.

775
00:52:49,500 --> 00:52:50,835
What about you, Sir Enzo?

776
00:52:51,335 --> 00:52:52,336
Wait.

777
00:52:54,046 --> 00:52:55,590
There are no messages from her.

778
00:52:57,800 --> 00:52:58,801
That's weird.

779
00:52:59,218 --> 00:53:01,596
She'd usually inform us
if she won't come to work, right?

780
00:53:01,679 --> 00:53:03,514
Actually, yes.

781
00:53:04,473 --> 00:53:06,559
She just probably woke up late.

782
00:53:07,810 --> 00:53:09,604
Enzo, Mom is never late.

783
00:53:09,896 --> 00:53:12,607
She's almost always the first one
to arrive here.

784
00:53:12,690 --> 00:53:14,066
-Take these to the laundry room.
-Okay. All right.

785
00:53:14,150 --> 00:53:15,151
Thank you.

786
00:53:19,989 --> 00:53:21,574
-Hello?
-Hello, Nanny Cora?

787
00:53:22,450 --> 00:53:23,534
Is Mom there?

788
00:53:23,618 --> 00:53:24,785
No, she's not here.

789
00:53:25,161 --> 00:53:26,495
She didn't come home last night.

790
00:53:27,705 --> 00:53:28,873
Why?

791
00:53:28,956 --> 00:53:32,585
She had Benjie drive her somewhere,
then sent him home.

792
00:53:33,044 --> 00:53:34,545
Did she say where she's going?

793
00:53:34,921 --> 00:53:36,589
To Ricardo's house.

794
00:53:57,234 --> 00:53:58,778
Patricia isn't with you?

795
00:54:02,740 --> 00:54:03,616
No.

796
00:54:04,784 --> 00:54:07,745
I didn't see her all day.
I think she's avoiding me.

797
00:54:08,412 --> 00:54:09,997
She's still upset with me.

798
00:54:10,331 --> 00:54:12,083
But I can't blame her.

799
00:54:12,375 --> 00:54:14,752
If I was in her place, I'd get upset too.

800
00:54:15,086 --> 00:54:18,547
If I had just told her
when she was younger,

801
00:54:19,090 --> 00:54:20,883
maybe she wouldn't get hurt this much.

802
00:54:21,258 --> 00:54:26,222
Are you saying it's wrong
for us to be together?

803
00:54:26,305 --> 00:54:29,350
-Carlota…
-The way I see it,

804
00:54:29,433 --> 00:54:32,436
you regret ever being with me!

805
00:54:32,520 --> 00:54:33,938
I never said anything like that.

806
00:54:34,021 --> 00:54:36,899
You never say it,
but that's what you think, right?

807
00:54:38,025 --> 00:54:41,487
It's exhausting waiting for you
to choose me for once!

808
00:54:42,238 --> 00:54:46,117
You know what I went through
with Diana's family!

809
00:54:47,034 --> 00:54:49,954
I've looked up to them
since I was a child,

810
00:54:50,037 --> 00:54:52,498
especially to Diana herself.

811
00:54:53,582 --> 00:54:56,043
Then, you came into my life.

812
00:54:56,544 --> 00:54:59,463
And even with you,
I still feel like a beggar!

813
00:55:00,047 --> 00:55:03,843
I thought I could have you
all for myself, Martin!

814
00:55:04,176 --> 00:55:06,303
That we can have a happy family together…

815
00:55:06,554 --> 00:55:08,389
but I was wrong.

816
00:55:12,018 --> 00:55:13,019
Carlota…

817
00:55:17,773 --> 00:55:20,109
Hey, Patricia, everything will be fine.

818
00:55:20,651 --> 00:55:22,486
The police are on standby

819
00:55:23,195 --> 00:55:25,906
in case Ms. D doesn't respond
within tonight.

820
00:55:25,990 --> 00:55:29,285
Why won't she tell us where she is?

821
00:55:32,038 --> 00:55:33,080
Come here.

822
00:55:34,749 --> 00:55:35,750
Hey…

823
00:55:37,460 --> 00:55:39,670
Don't worry too much, okay?

824
00:55:49,221 --> 00:55:50,306
Patricia?

825
00:55:55,644 --> 00:55:57,396
Sir, good evening.

826
00:56:03,069 --> 00:56:05,654
"I'LL EXPLAIN EVERYTHING, DEAR.
WE'LL TALK WHEN I GET HOME."

827
00:56:06,947 --> 00:56:08,741
-It's Mom.
-Why?

828
00:56:09,450 --> 00:56:10,951
What happened to Diana?

829
00:56:32,932 --> 00:56:33,933
Boss.

830
00:56:38,145 --> 00:56:40,564
Find out what Ricardo has to do

831
00:56:40,731 --> 00:56:42,650
with Cecilia Pineda.

832
00:56:43,526 --> 00:56:45,611
And I want this information
as soon as possible.

833
00:56:45,694 --> 00:56:46,862
Copy, boss.

834
00:56:56,705 --> 00:56:57,706
Mom!

835
00:56:58,541 --> 00:56:59,542
Patricia.

836
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:02,878
What happened to you?
You were gone for days!

837
00:57:03,546 --> 00:57:05,798
I'm fine, dear. I'm fine.

838
00:57:06,549 --> 00:57:08,342
What's the important thing
we need to talk about?

839
00:57:08,884 --> 00:57:09,802
Diana!

840
00:57:10,469 --> 00:57:11,470
What's this nonsense?

841
00:57:12,888 --> 00:57:13,931
I was worried--

842
00:57:15,766 --> 00:57:17,059
Patricia was worried sick!

843
00:57:17,560 --> 00:57:18,644
Take it easy, Martin.

844
00:57:19,186 --> 00:57:21,021
What did you do to Diana?

845
00:57:24,483 --> 00:57:26,152
We only wanted to talk with Patricia.

846
00:57:26,402 --> 00:57:27,403
You little…

847
00:57:27,486 --> 00:57:30,656
Sir? We don't need
to make a scene here, please.

848
00:57:33,701 --> 00:57:36,078
Whatever you need to tell Patricia,

849
00:57:36,162 --> 00:57:37,163
I need to know, too.

850
00:57:37,496 --> 00:57:40,791
I'm not leaving without my daughter.

851
00:57:40,875 --> 00:57:44,962
And I won't shut up until you speak.

852
00:57:45,212 --> 00:57:46,505
This is a family matter.

853
00:57:47,840 --> 00:57:49,550
You arrogant bastard.

854
00:57:50,009 --> 00:57:51,594
-Who do you think you are?
-Sir!

855
00:57:51,677 --> 00:57:52,887
Martin.

856
00:57:58,642 --> 00:58:00,144
Let go of my husband.

857
00:58:19,580 --> 00:58:20,623
We're married.

858
00:58:27,213 --> 00:58:29,215
UNCLE TEDDY

859
00:58:44,146 --> 00:58:45,981
I hope you will be happy for us.

860
00:58:46,065 --> 00:58:47,691
Because I'm happy.

861
00:58:47,775 --> 00:58:49,860
If something needs to be hidden,

862
00:58:49,944 --> 00:58:51,737
that means something is wrong with it.

863
00:58:51,820 --> 00:58:52,905
The way she acts right now…

864
00:58:53,197 --> 00:58:54,949
Very out of character for her.

865
00:58:55,032 --> 00:58:57,660
If Mom loves and trusts you,

866
00:58:57,743 --> 00:58:58,744
don't expect the same from me.

867
00:58:58,827 --> 00:59:01,205
Patricia, I am not the enemy.

868
00:59:01,580 --> 00:59:03,082
-Is Diana there?
-Yes.

869
00:59:03,165 --> 00:59:04,333
Don't let her leave.

870
00:59:04,416 --> 00:59:05,584
There's something she needs to know.

871
00:59:05,668 --> 00:59:07,753
I want you to be happy,

872
00:59:08,045 --> 00:59:10,965
but I also want you to be safe.
